      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Iceberg in Snowflake\nHow does Snowflake work with\nIceberg tables, and where does\nSnowflake Open Catalog fit?\nSnowflake can be the catalog for\nan Iceberg table, or it can use\ntables that another catalog owns.\nSnowflake Open Catalog is a\nseparate catalog service that many\nengines can share.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 22.5,
      "containerId": "node-1da7fd9b9469",
      "originalText": "Iceberg in Snowflake\nHow does Snowflake work with Iceberg tables, and where does Snowflake Open Catalog fit? Snowflake can be the catalog for an Iceberg table, or it can use tables that another catalog owns. Snowflake Open Catalog is a separate catalog service that many engines can share.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "snowflake-iceberg"
      }
    },
