    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5389168862,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-27ac4ccb708f",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1094.4,
      "y": 446.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 184.8,
      "height": 875.0,
      "seed": 932731,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Snowflake Open Catalog\nSnowflake Open Catalog\nis Snowflake's hosted\nversion of Apache\nPolaris, an\nopen-source Iceberg\nREST catalog. Its job\nis to give many\nengines read and write\naccess to the same\nIceberg tables.\nSnowflake, Spark,\nFlink, Trino, and a\nKafka sink connector\ncan all use it.\n\nIt is a Snowflake\naccount of its own\ntype, with its own web\ninterface, users, and\nprincipals. An\norganization\nadministrator creates\nit in Snowsight, under\nAdmin > Accounts, or\nwith CREATE ACCOUNT\n... POLARIS = TRUE.\nIts REST endpoint has\nthe form https://<org>\n-<account>.snowflakeco\nmputing.com/polaris/ap\ni/catalog.\n\nIt is probably\nseparate because its\nclients are other\nengines, which need\nonly a catalog API and\nidentities of their\nown. As of November\n2026, only\norganizations that\nalready have an Open\nCatalog account can\ncreate more. The [Open\nCatalog overview](http\ns://docs.snowflake.com\n/en/user-guide/opencat\nalog/overview)\ndescribes the service.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-27ac4ccb708f",
      "originalText": "Snowflake Open Catalog\nSnowflake Open Catalog is Snowflake's hosted version of Apache Polaris, an open-source Iceberg REST catalog. Its job is to give many engines read and write access to the same Iceberg tables. Snowflake, Spark, Flink, Trino, and a Kafka sink connector can all use it.\n\nIt is a Snowflake account of its own type, with its own web interface, users, and principals. An organization administrator creates it in Snowsight, under Admin > Accounts, or with CREATE ACCOUNT ... POLARIS = TRUE. Its REST endpoint has the form https://<org>-<account>.snowflakecomputing.com/polaris/api/catalog.\n\nIt is probably separate because its clients are other engines, which need only a catalog API and identities of their own. As of November 2026, only organizations that already have an Open Catalog account can create more. The [Open Catalog overview](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/opencatalog/overview) describes the service.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "snowflake-open-catalog"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5146488468,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-8196d2dacc03",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1082.4,
      "y": 527.5,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 276.0,
      "height": 41.5,
      "seed": 419120,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
        "value": 8
      },
      "boundElements": [
